1
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,410
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:35,190 --> 00:01:37,200
The second and third Ashino Lakes,

37
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,450
I hope there won't be any more of those.

38
00:01:40,530 --> 00:01:44,290
I received a complaint from
Chairman Kiel about the delay.

39
00:01:44,290 --> 00:01:45,750
It came directly to me.

40
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:51,380
He was pretty upset.
He even hinted at dismissing you.

41
00:01:51,790 --> 00:01:53,760
Adam is proceeding well,

42
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:56,590
and the Eva Project has begun work
on the dummy plugs.

43
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,760
What do the old men of Seele
have to complain about?

44
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:02,720
The all-important Human Instrumentality Project
is behind schedule.

45
00:02:03,430 --> 00:02:07,270
All the projects are linked.
There are no problems.

46
00:02:07,270 --> 00:02:08,850
Including Rei?

47
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:11,150
Well, never mind.

48
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:14,440
By the way, what should we do about that man?

49
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:18,110
We'll leave him to his own devices.
The same with the Marduk Institute.

50
00:02:18,110 --> 00:02:20,910
I suppose we'll let him work to our purposes
for a while longer.

51
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:24,660
KYOTO

52
00:02:24,950 --> 00:02:28,370
What started here, sixteen years ago?

53
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:47,770
EPISODE 15
LIES AND SILENCE

54
00:02:50,650 --> 00:02:52,440
It's me.

55
00:02:53,770 --> 00:02:55,190
Yes, so it is.

56
00:02:56,070 --> 00:02:59,700
Shannon Bio, a chemical firm
funded from overseas.

57
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:04,910
It's been here for nine years,
but it also hasn't changed in nine years.

58
00:03:05,490 --> 00:03:09,040
The Marduk Institute has
108 affiliated companies.

59
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:11,210
106 of them turned out to be
dummy corporations.

60
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:13,500
And this is the 107th?

61
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:16,000
This is the corporate registration.

62
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,300
You want me to take a look
at the board of directors, right?

63
00:03:18,630 --> 00:03:22,010
Gendo Ikari

64
00:03:18,630 --> 00:03:22,010
Kouzou Fuyutsuki

65
00:03:18,630 --> 00:03:22,010
Kiel Lorenz

66
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:20,510
So you already knew about it?

67
00:03:20,510 --> 00:03:22,550
The names are all familiar.

68
00:03:22,550 --> 00:03:27,350
The Marduk Institute is supposed to be
an advisory body

69
00:03:27,350 --> 00:03:30,600
controlled by the Human Instrumentality
Committee to select Eva pilots.

70
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,850
What it really does is not clear.

71
00:03:32,850 --> 00:03:35,730
Your duty is to investigate Nerv.

72
00:03:35,730 --> 00:03:38,110
Getting involved in the Marduk Institute
is a bad idea.

73
00:03:38,110 --> 00:03:43,610
Well, I'm the type that has to see
everything for myself.

74
00:03:44,910 --> 00:03:48,290
Hi, this is Kaji. I'm out right now.

75
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:51,000
Please leave your name and message.

76
00:03:53,790 --> 00:03:57,500
Help me, Mr. Kaji! Don't touch me, you pervert!

77
00:03:58,670 --> 00:04:00,670
Not.

78
00:04:00,670 --> 00:04:02,430
What's going on?

79
00:04:02,430 --> 00:04:04,220
Well, tomorrow's Sunday.

80
00:04:04,590 --> 00:04:10,560
So I called Mr. Kaji, thinking that I'd get him
to take me out somewhere, but he's not in.

81
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:13,810
He's always out lately, no matter when I call.

82
00:04:13,810 --> 00:04:15,480
That means you're free tomorrow, right?

83
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:18,820
Regrettably, yes.

84
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:21,900
Then I have a little favor to ask of you.

85
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:23,950
Well, it's like this...

86
00:04:25,490 --> 00:04:28,160
What?! A date?!

87
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:30,330
A friend of my big sister Kodama

88
00:04:30,330 --> 00:04:33,120
is insisting that I introduce you to him.

89
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:34,420
Please!

90
00:04:46,890 --> 00:04:48,350
Head!

91
00:04:48,350 --> 00:04:50,180
Get to it!

92
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:51,060
I'm sorry.

93
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:53,310
YOU need to get to it and clean!

94
00:04:53,310 --> 00:04:55,230
Necrosis operation complete.

95
00:04:55,230 --> 00:04:57,020
Graph measurement complete.

96
00:04:57,020 --> 00:04:59,150
What are you going to wear tomorrow?
Synch rate is normal.

97
00:04:59,150 --> 00:05:01,230
Oh, to the wedding?

98
00:05:01,230 --> 00:05:04,360
I wore the pink suit for Kiyomi's wedding,

99
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:07,370
and the dark blue dress for Kotoko's
just the other day.

100
00:05:07,370 --> 00:05:08,530
What about the orange one?

101
00:05:08,530 --> 00:05:10,080
You haven't worn that one lately, have you?

102
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:13,330
Well, there's a reason for that.

103
00:05:13,330 --> 00:05:14,620
It's too tight?

104
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:16,210
Yeah, so what?!

105
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,580
Should I get a new one on the way home?

106
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:22,380
It's an extra expense.

107
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:26,630
We've been invited to so many weddings lately,
the cost of all the gifts is starting to add up.

108
00:05:26,630 --> 00:05:30,560
Everyone's just rushing to get married
before they're thirty.

109
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:33,680
No one wants to be the last one still single.

110
00:05:34,310 --> 00:05:36,730
That's enough, you three.

111
00:05:36,730 --> 00:05:38,310
Good work.

112
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:41,020
All these stupid tests are boring!

113
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:48,660
By the way, Shinji looks even more
downcast than usual today.

114
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:50,990
That's because of tomorrow.

115
00:05:51,450 --> 00:05:53,330
Yes, tomorrow.

116
00:05:54,330 --> 00:05:57,790
Tomorrow, I have to see my father.

117
00:05:59,630 --> 00:06:02,210
What should I talk to him about?

118
00:06:02,210 --> 00:06:04,760
Why do you ask me?

119
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:08,590
Because I once saw you
talking happily with him.

120
00:06:11,550 --> 00:06:15,310
Say, what kind of person is my father?

121
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:18,690
I don't know.

122
00:06:20,810 --> 00:06:22,020
I see.

123
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:25,530
You've been looking at me all afternoon
because you wanted to ask me that?

124
00:06:27,190 --> 00:06:32,200
When we were cleaning today,
you were wringing out the cloth, remember?

125
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,620
The way you did it was like a mother.

126
00:06:35,330 --> 00:06:37,040
A mother?

127
00:06:39,210 --> 00:06:43,630
I thought it was like a mother.

128
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:48,220
Maybe you'd be really good
at being a housewife, Ayanami.

129
00:06:51,430 --> 00:06:52,970
What are you saying?!

130
00:06:54,850 --> 00:06:59,100
<i><i>What do you mean? You're the one
that wanted to break up!</i></i>

131
00:06:57,390 --> 00:06:59,100
I'm home.

132
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:00,480
Welcome back.

133
00:06:59,270 --> 00:07:03,690
<i><i>I was wrong. I wasn't thinking back then.</i></i>

134
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:03,770
You'd better go to bed.
Aren't you going on a date tomorrow?

135
00:07:03,690 --> 00:07:05,820
<i><i>What are you saying at this late date?</i></i>

136
00:07:03,770 --> 00:07:05,820
Yeah, with a hunk.

137
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:09,610
<i><i>I don't know about you,
but I'm a different person now!</i></i>

138
00:07:06,690 --> 00:07:10,200
Hey, that's right, let me use
your lavender perfume!

139
00:07:09,610 --> 00:07:12,110
<i><i>But I still love you!</i></i>

140
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,160
Absolutely not.

141
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:13,160
Jeez, cheapskate!

142
00:07:12,110 --> 00:07:15,620
<i><i>Time and people are two things that can't be
turned back to the way they were!</i></i>

143
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:15,450
It's not for kids.

144
00:07:15,450 --> 00:07:16,540
Is Shinji in his room?

145
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:18,000
<i><i>I can never go back to the way I was!</i></i>

146
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:18,160
He's been in there since he got back.

147
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,830
<i><i>But I really do still love you!</i></i>

148
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:20,210
It looks like he doesn't want to see his father.

149
00:07:19,830 --> 00:07:22,330
<i><i>I'm telling you, it's impossible!</i></i>

150
00:07:20,210 --> 00:07:22,000
If he doesn't want to, he should just say so.

151
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,170
I don't understand the Japanese.

152
00:07:22,330 --> 00:07:27,880
<i><i>It took me three years to forget you! It's too late!</i></i>

153
00:07:24,170 --> 00:07:26,380
Well, it's not that he doesn't want to.

154
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:28,460
That's the problem.

155
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:34,760
Leave!

156
00:07:39,350 --> 00:07:42,400
Well done, Shinji.

157
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:47,110
Shinji?

158
00:07:47,110 --> 00:07:48,690
I'm opening the door.

159
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:55,320
Are you scared? Of seeing
your father by yourself?

160
00:07:57,030 --> 00:07:59,200
You can't keep running away.

161
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:02,080
Unless you take that step forward,
nothing will change.

162
00:08:02,710 --> 00:08:04,460
I know that!

163
00:08:05,130 --> 00:08:07,000
You'll begin to realize,

164
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:11,510
after that first step, it's just as important
to keep going.

165
00:08:12,130 --> 00:08:15,470
Anyway, go see him tomorrow
with your chin held high,

166
00:08:15,470 --> 00:08:17,140
because you'll be seeing your mother too.

167
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:19,430
Well, good night.

168
00:08:24,980 --> 00:08:28,190
Hey, you bought a new dress for tomorrow,
didn't you? Let me see!

169
00:08:28,190 --> 00:08:30,530
Oh, you want to see?
It was expensive, you know.

170
00:08:30,530 --> 00:08:32,070
Taste is more important than price.

171
00:08:32,070 --> 00:08:33,740
I've got that down pat.

172
00:08:33,740 --> 00:08:37,620
Did you pick based on Mr. Kaji's
taste and stuff after all?

173
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:39,410
I think not. Not anymore.

174
00:08:39,450 --> 00:08:41,120
NEXT DAY

175
00:08:41,290 --> 00:08:41,830
Well!

176
00:08:41,830 --> 00:08:42,460
See you...

177
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:43,040
Later.

178
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:51,920
<i>Place three bags in your heart...</i>

179
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:55,130
<i>Red, blue, and yellow...</i>

180
00:08:55,130 --> 00:08:57,340
Now let us proceed with the reception.

181
00:08:57,340 --> 00:08:58,220
Mr. Ryoji Kaji

182
00:08:59,850 --> 00:09:01,430
Ryo's late.

183
00:09:01,430 --> 00:09:05,310
That idiot has never been on time
in his entire life!

184
00:09:05,310 --> 00:09:08,610
For your dates, you mean?
He's always on time for work.

185
00:09:08,610 --> 00:09:12,320
Hey, you two! You look
even more beautiful today.

186
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:14,650
I couldn't get off work in time.

187
00:09:14,650 --> 00:09:16,910
As if you're not puttering
around the office all the time.

188
00:09:17,870 --> 00:09:21,160
Not that I care, but couldn't you have done
something about that stubble?

189
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:23,000
Look, your necktie is crooked.

190
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:25,460
Well, thank you.

191
00:09:25,460 --> 00:09:27,330
You two act like you're married.

192
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:29,500
Sounds good to me, Ritchan.

193
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:30,670
Like hell I'd take him.

194
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:49,060
It's been three years since the last time
we came here together.

195
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:52,360
I ran away then,

196
00:09:52,690 --> 00:09:54,820
and haven't been back since.

197
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:59,240
It just hasn't sunk in that Mother is resting here.

198
00:09:59,240 --> 00:10:00,950
I don't even remember her face.

199
00:10:00,950 --> 00:10:03,990
Man survives by forgetting his memories,

200
00:10:03,990 --> 00:10:07,000
but there are some things
a man should never forget.

201
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,500
Yui taught me about the irreplaceable things.

202
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:13,750
I come here to confirm that.

203
00:10:15,590 --> 00:10:17,260
You have no pictures of her?

204
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:18,760
There are none left.

205
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:21,720
This grave is just a decoration too.
There's no corpse.

206
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:25,850
So, the teacher was right.
You threw them all away.

207
00:10:25,850 --> 00:10:28,850
I keep everything in my heart.
That is enough for now.

208
00:10:32,230 --> 00:10:34,230
It's time. I'm leaving now.

209
00:10:41,910 --> 00:10:42,580
Father!

210
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:49,210
Um, I'm glad I got to talk to you today.

211
00:10:50,080 --> 00:10:51,960
I see.

212
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:39,720
Not bad! I didn't know you played.

213
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:43,180
I've been studying since I was five,
and this is all I can do,

214
00:11:43,180 --> 00:11:44,890
so I don't really have any talent.

215
00:11:44,890 --> 00:11:48,100
Perseverance is power. I'm a little impressed.

216
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:50,350
I started studying because
my teacher told me to,

217
00:11:50,350 --> 00:11:51,980
so I could have quit anytime.

218
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:54,440
Then why did you keep going?

219
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:56,520
Because nobody told me to stop.

220
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:58,780
I should have known!

221
00:11:58,780 --> 00:12:02,320
You came back early.
I thought you'd have dinner too.

222
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:04,620
He was just so boring!

223
00:12:04,620 --> 00:12:09,160
So, while he was waiting in line
for the roller coaster, I left.

224
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:11,000
That doesn't seem too nice.

225
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:14,710
Really, Mr. Kaji is the only real man around.

226
00:12:16,090 --> 00:12:18,670
What're you saying after all this time?

227
00:12:18,670 --> 00:12:20,920
I'm ducking out to the restroom.

228
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:22,130
Don't ditch me now!

229
00:12:27,550 --> 00:12:29,680
High heels...

230
00:12:29,680 --> 00:12:32,770
How many years has it been since
the three of us last drank together?

231
00:12:32,770 --> 00:12:34,520
Isn't Misato drinking too much?

232
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:36,690
She's acting a little giddy.

233
00:12:36,690 --> 00:12:40,030
And you drink some more to
keep your high spirits in check.

234
00:12:40,570 --> 00:12:42,440
Or vice versa, today.

235
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:46,160
As someone who lived with her,
your words carry the weight of truth.

236
00:12:46,530 --> 00:12:48,280
Well, I did live with her,

237
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:51,200
but that was before she started
wearing heels and things.

238
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:54,250
It was unimaginable when
we were back in school.

239
00:12:54,250 --> 00:12:56,130
I was a brat too.

240
00:12:56,130 --> 00:13:01,050
That wasn't really sharing a life.
It was just living together, playing house.

241
00:13:01,050 --> 00:13:03,170
Reality isn't that easy.

242
00:13:03,170 --> 00:13:05,680
Oh yeah, here. A cat souvenir.

243
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:07,970
My, thank you. You're very thorough.

244
00:13:07,970 --> 00:13:10,560
Only with the ladies.
When it comes to work, I'm sloppy.

245
00:13:10,560 --> 00:13:12,470
I somehow doubt that.

246
00:13:12,470 --> 00:13:13,730
What about for Misato?

247
00:13:13,730 --> 00:13:15,390
I lost once before.

248
00:13:15,390 --> 00:13:17,520
I make a point of not fighting
when I can't win the battle.

249
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:19,360
I think you have a chance at victory.

250
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,570
What about you?

251
00:13:20,570 --> 00:13:22,990
I make a point of not talking about myself,

252
00:13:22,990 --> 00:13:24,110
because it's no fun.

253
00:13:25,110 --> 00:13:28,740
Katsuragi's sure taking a long time.
Maybe she's fixing her make-up?

254
00:13:29,370 --> 00:13:32,040
What were you doing in Kyoto?

255
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:34,460
Huh? That's from Matsushiro.

256
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:35,870
It's no use playing dumb.

257
00:13:35,870 --> 00:13:38,670
Your fingers will get burned if you
get involved in this too deeply.

258
00:13:38,670 --> 00:13:41,250
That's the advice of a friend.

259
00:13:41,250 --> 00:13:43,010
I'll take it seriously,

260
00:13:43,010 --> 00:13:46,340
but if I have to get burned, I'd rather be burned
while playing with fire along with you.

261
00:13:45,130 --> 00:13:47,550
Shall I go buy you some fireworks?

262
00:13:47,550 --> 00:13:48,550
Welcome back!

263
00:13:48,550 --> 00:13:50,930
You haven't changed, have you, you player?

264
00:13:50,930 --> 00:13:55,060
Of course I've changed. To live is to change.

265
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:57,690
Homeostasis and transistasis.

266
00:13:57,690 --> 00:13:58,690
What are those?

267
00:13:58,690 --> 00:14:01,770
One is a force for the status quo,
and the other's a force for change.

268
00:14:01,770 --> 00:14:06,030
A living thing is something that has
both of these conflicting qualities.

269
00:14:06,030 --> 00:14:07,860
Like men and women.

270
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:11,370
Well, I'll be leaving now.
I've still got some work to do.

271
00:14:11,370 --> 00:14:12,530
Really?

272
00:14:12,530 --> 00:14:13,790
Sorry to hear it.

273
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:15,370
Later.

274
00:14:22,670 --> 00:14:25,840
Hey, Shin? It's me.

275
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:29,760
I'm drinking with Kaji right now.
Right, we're on the third after-party.

276
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:33,060
Yes... Okay, later.

277
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:34,060
Was it Misato?

278
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:37,100
Yes, she said she'll be late,
so don't wait up for her.

279
00:14:37,100 --> 00:14:40,150
What? Don't tell me she's coming back
in the morning!

280
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:42,610
No way, she's with Mr. Kaji.

281
00:14:42,610 --> 00:14:44,940
What are you, stupid? That's WHY!

282
00:14:51,030 --> 00:14:53,330
You shouldn't be throwing up at your age.

283
00:14:53,330 --> 00:14:56,160
So sorry I'm that age.

284
00:14:56,160 --> 00:14:57,790
I guess we're both that age.

285
00:14:57,790 --> 00:14:59,290
Damn right.

286
00:14:59,290 --> 00:15:02,170
You're wearing heels now, after all.

287
00:15:02,170 --> 00:15:03,500
Time's really flown.

288
00:15:04,460 --> 00:15:07,130
Shave that stubble off.

289
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:08,920
Yes, Ma'am.

290
00:15:09,340 --> 00:15:11,680
I'll walk the rest of the way. Thanks.

291
00:15:16,430 --> 00:15:19,770
Kaji, do you think I've changed?

292
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:22,230
You've become more beautiful.

293
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:27,820
I'm sorry that I insisted on
breaking up with you.

294
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:30,780
When I said I fell in love with somebody else,

295
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:33,160
that was a lie. Did you know?

296
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:34,740
No.

297
00:15:36,910 --> 00:15:39,040
It's just that I realized

298
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:42,080
you were like my father.

299
00:15:44,630 --> 00:15:50,010
That I wanted a man like my father...

300
00:15:50,010 --> 00:15:53,220
When I realized that, I was afraid.

301
00:15:53,510 --> 00:15:55,640
I was desperately afraid.

302
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:58,890
Of being with you, Kaji...

303
00:15:58,890 --> 00:16:01,270
Of being a woman...

304
00:16:01,270 --> 00:16:03,980
I was afraid of everything.

305
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:09,230
I hated my father, but fell in love
with someone just like him.

306
00:16:10,110 --> 00:16:13,110
I chose Nerv, intending to
make a clean break with the past.

307
00:16:13,660 --> 00:16:16,700
But even that was an organization
that Father used to belong to.

308
00:16:16,700 --> 00:16:21,210
In the end, I've been fooling myself
by taking revenge against the Angels.

309
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:29,170
That was your decision, Katsuragi.

310
00:16:29,170 --> 00:16:31,260
You don't have to apologize to me.

311
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:34,050
No, that wasn't a decision!

312
00:16:34,050 --> 00:16:36,430
I was just running away.

313
00:16:36,430 --> 00:16:39,220
Running away from the snare of my father!

314
00:16:39,220 --> 00:16:41,770
I'm just like Shinji.

315
00:16:41,770 --> 00:16:43,350
I'm a coward.

316
00:16:44,230 --> 00:16:48,400
I'm really sorry. Telling you all this now
because I drank too much...

317
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:49,360
That's enough.

318
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,110
I'm such a child.

319
00:16:51,110 --> 00:16:53,450
I have no right to tell Shinji anything.

320
00:16:53,450 --> 00:16:54,450
That's enough!

321
00:16:54,450 --> 00:16:59,450
On top of that, I'm an underhanded woman
that just clings to men when it suits me!

322
00:16:59,450 --> 00:17:02,790
Even back then, I may have just been using you!

323
00:17:02,790 --> 00:17:04,410
I hate myself!

324
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:05,210
That's enough! Stop it!

325
00:17:04,710 --> 00:17:07,170
I'm so pathetic!

326
00:17:30,190 --> 00:17:33,900
Hey, Shinji, do you want to kiss?

327
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:34,360
What?

328
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:37,110
A kiss. A kiss? You've never kissed, right?

329
00:17:38,950 --> 00:17:40,620
Then, let's do it.

330
00:17:40,620 --> 00:17:41,330
Why?

331
00:17:41,330 --> 00:17:42,950
Because I'm bored.

332
00:17:42,950 --> 00:17:45,790
Because you're bored?! But...

333
00:17:45,790 --> 00:17:49,250
You don't want to kiss a girl on
the anniversary of your mom's death?

334
00:17:49,250 --> 00:17:51,920
Afraid she may be watching you from Heaven?

335
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:52,630
Not really.

336
00:17:52,630 --> 00:17:54,010
Or are you scared?

337
00:17:54,010 --> 00:17:56,090
I'm not scared of a little kiss!

338
00:17:56,090 --> 00:17:58,140
You brushed your teeth, didn't you?

339
00:17:59,090 --> 00:18:00,800
Then, here I go.

340
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:12,860
Don't breathe, because it tickles.

341
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:01,570
Definitely not something to do to kill time!

342
00:19:05,540 --> 00:19:07,870
All right, here we are. Hang on.

343
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:11,380
Mr. Kaji!

344
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:12,710
What?!

345
00:19:13,590 --> 00:19:14,500
Mr. Kaji!

346
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:20,510
Well, I'll be leaving now.

347
00:19:20,510 --> 00:19:22,430
Why don't you stay with us, Kaji?

348
00:19:22,430 --> 00:19:25,100
I'd be laughed at if I went to work in this.

349
00:19:26,260 --> 00:19:28,060
It'll be okay.

350
00:19:28,060 --> 00:19:30,980
Hey, c'mon, Mr. Kaji...

351
00:19:30,980 --> 00:19:32,480
Later.

352
00:19:36,150 --> 00:19:38,150
He smelled of lavender...

353
00:19:39,190 --> 00:19:42,160
Please take care of Katsuragi.

354
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:43,160
Sure.

355
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:44,200
Well, 'night.

356
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:45,780
Good night.

357
00:19:47,990 --> 00:19:50,460
What's wrong? You look down.

358
00:19:50,460 --> 00:19:52,960
It's because I kissed you!

359
00:19:53,830 --> 00:19:58,590
Well, let me call the girl's roll. Ayanami...

360
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:55,420
NEXT DAY

361
00:19:58,590 --> 00:20:01,630
Oh, Ayanami's absent again?

362
00:20:03,050 --> 00:20:03,760
NERV HEADQUARTERS

363
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:05,260
DEEP UNDERGROUND FACILITY
CENTRAL AREA

364
00:20:05,350 --> 00:20:06,260
CENTRAL DOGMA

365
00:20:27,370 --> 00:20:29,410
2008 METERS UNDERGROUND

366
00:20:29,490 --> 00:20:31,200
TERMINAL DOGMA

367
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:45,300
Hi, how's your hangover?

368
00:20:45,300 --> 00:20:46,850
I'm finally sober now, thanks.

369
00:20:46,850 --> 00:20:47,970
Glad to hear it.

370
00:20:47,970 --> 00:20:51,810
Is this your day job, or your side job?

371
00:20:51,810 --> 00:20:52,890
I wonder which?

372
00:20:52,890 --> 00:20:56,690
Ryoji Kaji of Special Duty Organization Nerv's
Special Inspection Department...

373
00:20:56,690 --> 00:21:01,610
Also, Ryoji Kaji of the Investigation Department
of the Japanese Ministry of Home Affairs.

374
00:21:01,610 --> 00:21:02,690
So you know all about it.

375
00:21:02,690 --> 00:21:04,910
Don't underestimate Nerv.

376
00:21:04,910 --> 00:21:06,740
Is this an order from Commander Ikari?

377
00:21:06,740 --> 00:21:08,200
My own discretion.

378
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:11,330
If you keep doing this other job, you'll die.

379
00:21:11,330 --> 00:21:14,540
Commander Ikari is using me.
I can still keep going.

380
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:18,340
However, I will apologize for hiding it from you.

381
00:21:18,340 --> 00:21:20,750
I'll call it even in thanks for yesterday.

382
00:21:20,750 --> 00:21:23,340
Thanks very much, but...

383
00:21:23,340 --> 00:21:27,260
The Commander and Ritchan are hiding
things from you too, and...

384
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:28,300
This is it.

385
00:21:34,770 --> 00:21:35,690
This is...

386
00:21:38,860 --> 00:21:40,650
Eva? No!

387
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,480
Impossible...

388
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:48,410
Yes, this is the origin and linchpin of
everything since the Second Impact.

389
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:50,410
This is Adam.

390
00:21:50,410 --> 00:21:53,410
Adam? The First Angel is here?

391
00:21:54,580 --> 00:21:55,870
You're right.

392
00:21:55,870 --> 00:21:59,000
Nerv is deeper in this than I thought.

393
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:00,590
TO BE CONTINUED

394
00:23:06,070 --> 00:23:06,940
PREVIEW

395
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:10,950
The puffed-up Shinji gets swallowed
in a Sea of Dirac.

396
00:23:10,950 --> 00:23:14,700
The short amount of time left to him
teaches him the meaning of despair.

397
00:23:14,700 --> 00:23:18,200
Next episode: "The Sickness Unto Death, And..."

398
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:20,460
More fan service next time!

399
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:21,040
THE SICKNESS UNTO DEATH, AND...
